AB  - In this preprint, we present the design, implementation, and evaluation of two domain-specific web applications augmented with Large Language Models (LLMs): MedMe, a telemedicine platform, and Wealth, an AI-powered personal finance management system. The study analyzes the potential of LLMs to enhance user experience, automate domain-specific workflows, and provide context-aware help in healthcare and finance. Both the systems are built using Next.js, Prisma ORM, PostgreSQL, Clerk authentication and Gemini API integration. The experimental evaluation reveals gains in task efficiency, automation and user satisfaction in both domains.
