TI  - Smarter Investing with AI: Using Neural Models to Personalize Financial Advice
AB  - Recent advances in Transformer-based neural architectures have catalyzed a new era of AI-driven financial advisory systems. Unlike traditional roboadvisors that rely on rule-based or shallow learning algorithms, Transformer models can process diverse financial and personal data to deliver personalized, context-aware investment guidance at scale. This paper explores the application of Transformers, particularly large language models (LLMs), in providing customized financial advice to individuals. We review the technical foundations of Transformers, propose a modular architecture for personalized advisory platforms, and analyze how user profiles, market data, and real-time financial behavior can be encoded to drive dynamic, user-specific recommendations. Real-world applications such as AI-powered robo-advisors, personal finance assistants, and autonomous trading agents are discussed, alongside the ethical, regulatory, and technological challenges they raise. We further highlight emerging research directions, including agentic AI, multi-modal personalization, explainability, and human-AI collaboration in financial services. Our findings suggest that Transformer-based personalization has the potential to democratize access to high-quality financial advice, but only if challenges related to privacy, trust, fairness, and compliance are carefully addressed.
