TI  - A Study on The Role of Generative AI In Personal Finance and Investment Decisions Among Salaried Individuals
AB  - Abstract The emergence of Generative Artificial Intelligence (Gen AI) has revolutionized the financial sector by providing personalized financial insights, automated budgeting solutions, investment recommendations, and risk assessment tools. Applications such as ChatGPT, Gemini, Microsoft Copilot, and AI-powered robo-advisors are increasingly being used by individuals for managing personal finances and making investment decisions. Salaried individuals, who represent a significant segment of investors, often seek efficient, accessible, and cost-effective financial planning solutions. Generative AI offers opportunities to improve financial literacy, enhance investment decision-making, and simplify wealth management. However, concerns related to accuracy, trustworthiness, privacy, and ethical considerations continue to influence adoption. This study investigates the role of Generative AI in personal finance and investment decisions among salaried individuals. The study examines awareness, usage patterns, perceived benefits, challenges, and trust in AI-generated financial advice. The findings contribute to understanding how AI technologies are reshaping personal financial management and investment behavior in the era of Industry 5.0.
