TI  - AI-Powered Personal Finance Assistant
AB  - This project presents an AI-powered personal finance assistant designed for users in Kazakhstan. The system addresses the difficulty of understanding personal spending patterns from local bank statements, which often vary in structure and are not fully supported by existing finance applications. The proposed solution combines a native iOS application, a FastAPI backend, a database layer, bank statement parsers, merchant normalization, automatic transaction categorization, financial dashboards, and an AI-assisted query interface. Users can upload bank statements from supported banks, after which the system extracts transactions, normalizes merchant descriptions, categorizes expenses, and visualizes spending through dashboards and budget-related views. The application also allows users to ask natural-language questions about their finances. The project was developed iteratively over two semesters. Key design decisions included migrating from React Native to SwiftUI, adopting a statement-first architecture instead of relying on direct bank integrations, and using a hybrid categorization approach that combines rule-based logic with lightweight machine learning. Evaluation results showed that the parser processed six supported bank statement files with 100% core-field completeness, while the transaction categorization model achieved 95.42% accuracy and 95.94% macro-F1 on the test set. Dashboard computations were completed in under one second, supporting interactive use within the prototype. Overall, the project demonstrates the feasibility of a localized, transparent, and AI-supported personal finance assistant for Kazakhstan users, while future work should expand bank support, improve chatbot robustness, strengthen security, and conduct broader user testing.
