TI  - Artificial Intelligence in Financial Literacy: Emerging Trends, Opportunities, and Challenges
AB  - Artificial Intelligence (AI) has come out as a revolutionary technology which is transforming many aspects of the global economy such as education, health care, finance, and banking. The use of AI in the financial sector can serve as a powerful means of enhancing financial literacy through the provision of user-friendly and personalized financial information. Financial literacy can be defined as the ability of an individual to have understanding as well as the skill and attitude for using financial information in order to make financial decisions regarding savings, investments, budgeting, borrowing, insurance, and retirement. Even though there have been advancements in financial services due to digitization, financial illiteracy remains a big problem especially in developing countries.AI helps to overcome these problems by offering personalized financial education, AI-enabled chatbots, robo-advisors, virtual financial assistants, predictive analytics, intelligent learning platforms that can help in simplifying complicated financial terms and help people make good financial decisions. The use of artificial intelligence can also help the financial institutions understand the financial behavior of their customers and find the areas where they lack in knowledge and offer customized financial education programs. Moreover, the use of AI with digital banking, mobile apps, and FinTechs has helped in improving financial inclusion and making financial services accessible to the underserved population.There are some challenges associated with the increasing use of AI for financial literacy, including data privacy issues, cyber security threats, algorithmic biases, digital inequality, ethical problems, and regulatory compliance issues.The current study is conceptual in its approach and is based on a descriptive type of research design wherein all the data have been obtained through secondary sources including scholarly articles, books, industrial reports, government documents, company reports, and credible websites. The research explores the importance of Artificial Intelligence in encouraging financial literacy and also discusses the recent trends, technological innovations, opportunities, challenges, and suggestions for policymakers, educators, financial institutions, and researchers. The results show that AI can make a positive change in the field of financial education through making it more accessible, personalized, aware, and knowledgeable.
