TI  - Quantum Finance: An AI-Assisted Personal Finance Management System
AB  - Personal finance apps typically require manual input of transactions. This can hinder the usability of personal finance managers. This paper introduces Quantum Finance, a personal finance manager with a web interface that reduces manual input. It uses computer vision and natural language processing to extract receipts, AI for categorizing expenses, budget monitoring with alerts, interactive dashboards, LLM generated insights and scheduled emails. The system is built using Next.js, TypeScript, Prisma ORM, PostgreSQL (Supabase), Clerk for authentication, Google Gemini API for multimodal tasks and text tasks, Inngest for background tasks and Resend for sending emails. The overall architecture, data flow and design of each section is discussed. Security, privacy and limitations of LLM content is also discussed. The system has only been functionally tested using example cases. Claims cannot be made regarding any quantitative testing on accuracy, time saving or user studies. Advanced features such as anomaly detection, forecasting and personal recommendations have been included but are purely future work.
