AB  - The effective use of generative artificial intelligence (GAI) in consumer finance research has attracted growing interest among scholars. This study demonstrates how GAI-specifically ChatGPT-can be applied to analyze financial literacy data and generate actionable insights. Using data from the National Financial Capability Study (NFCS), we show that ChatGPT can identify patterns, conduct meaningful analysis, and interpret key findings. Our results underscore the practical value of GAI as a tool for researchers, educators, and policymakers aiming to improve financial literacy through more targeted and accessible interventions, while also recognizing its limitations.
