AB  - Working paper describing CalcFi's methodology: how every calculator on calcfi.app is derived from US primary sources (IRS, BLS, BEA, FRED, U.S. Treasury, CFPB, HUD, Census, SSA, Freddie Mac PMMS), how reproducibility is enforced via versioned rate snapshots, and how the data layer is exposed via open REST APIs, an MCP server, and llms.txt for LLM-discovery. This record is part of the CalcFi open data archive, the citation surface for the CalcFi (calcfi.app) open finance calculator and US economic-data project. Every CalcFi calculator on the live site links to its primary source, and every rate series is versioned. This record is released under CC-BY 4.0. Primary data sources cited IRS · BLS · BEA · FRED · U.S. Treasury · CFPB · HUD · U.S. Census · SSA · Freddie Mac PMMS Related CalcFi surfaces Live site Methodology and provenance Developer documentation Open data hub Research outputs index Calculator registry (JSON) Live rate snapshot (JSON) LLM-discovery file Privacy and AI data practices CalcFi Zenodo community ORCID author profile MCP server on npm MCP server on PyPI Kaggle reproducibility notebooks Hugging Face Spaces How to cite @misc{calcfi_20260606, author={Salmisto, Jere}, title={CalcFi: Open Personal Finance Calculators and Cited US Economic Data}, year={2026}, url={https://calcfi.app} } License CC-BY 4.0. Attribution: CalcFi (calcfi.app). Disclaimer Educational use only. Not financial, tax, or legal advice. Maintainer Jere Salmisto (ORCID 0009-0000-0916-8684). hello@calcfi.app.
