TI  - Privacy-First Local Wealth Intelligence Terminal
AB  - Artificial Intelligence (AI) has revolutionized per-sonal finance management through automated budgeting, spend-ing analytics, real-time risk assessment, and personalized wealth creation strategies. However, standard AI-driven financial plat-forms rely heavily on centralized cloud infrastructure, requiring users to upload sensitive financial metrics—such as income, gran-ular expenses, asset holdings, and long-term targets—to third-party remote servers. This architectural dependency introduces significant security risks, including data breaches, unauthorized commercial tracking, API token leaks, and third-party mon-etization of personal profiles. Recent breakthroughs in open-weight quantized Large Language Models (LLMs) and optimized edge inference engines (e.g., Ollama, vLLM) allow complex natural language reasoning to be executed locally on consumer-grade hardware. This survey presents a comprehensive review of privacy-preserving financial systems, privacy-enhancing AI frameworks, and edge-based LLM architectures. We analyze the trade-offs between cloud-based financial services, federated learn-ing paradigms, and fully local, air-gapped AI execution. Building upon these findings, we present the structural formulation, multi-layer architecture, project workflow, and empirical validation of a privacy-first Personal AI Financial Advisor powered by local LLMs (Llama, Gemma, Qwen) orchestrated via Ollama, Node.js, Express, React, and local MongoDB storage. Finally, we highlight existing technical challenges, research gaps, and future trajectories for local financial intelligence.
