TI  - Artificial Intelligence in Banking: The Case of SBI Hyderabad
AB  - Artificial Intelligence (AI) has rapidly transformed the global banking industry, reshaping efficiency, security, and the overall customer experience in online banking. In India, the State Bank of India (SBI) stands as a pioneering example. As the largest public sector bank in the country, SBI has significantly enhanced its digital services by adopting AI-driven technologies such as chatbots, robo-advisors, biometric authentication, and fraud detection systems.Key innovations include the SBI Intelligent Assistant (SIA), Smart Assist, AskSBI, and Agentic AI—all of which have strengthened customer engagement, operational efficiency, and service personalization. These tools enable round-the-clock banking, real-time fraud detection, and automation of internal processes. The benefits of AI integration are clear: reduced costs, faster decision-making, improved service delivery, and expanded financial inclusion. Yet, challenges remain. Concerns such as job displacement, algorithmic biases, and data privacy risks highlight the need for careful regulation and ethical deployment. This study emphasizes that responsible innovation, backed by regulatory oversight and customer-centric strategies, is essential if AI is to serve both organizational goals and societal needs. Through its AI initiatives, SBI is not only modernizing its own operations but also contributing to India’s transition toward a safer, stronger, and more inclusive digital economy. For researchers, policymakers, and banking professionals, this case offers valuable insights into how AI is shaping the future of digital banking.
