TI  - AI driven digital transformation in sustainable green banking: a study on the impact of AI-powered FinTech innovations on banking efficiency and customer satisfaction
AB  - Artificial intelligence (AI) in the banking sector transforms conventional financial services by enhancing operational efficiency, improving customer experience. This study examines how AI enhances sustainable green banking in Indian commercial banks by improving efficiency, customer satisfaction, and environmental responsibility. Using primary data from 385 customers across SBI, HDFC, ICICI, PNB, and Axis Bank, the research employed SPSS-based analyses including regression, ANOVA, and factor analysis and model fit. Results show 65% of respondents reported faster, more secure services due to AI tools such as chatbots, automated credit systems, and fraud detection. A strong positive relationship was found between AI adoption and customer satisfaction (adjusted R2 = 0.819). Demographic factors like gender, income, education, and region influenced AI perceptions. Five key factors emerged: personal finance management, trust, investment advice, security, and efficiency. The study recommends transparent, personalised AI strategies, stronger privacy safeguards, and algorithmic fairness to build customer trust and promote sustainability in banking.
