TI  - Trends in the Digital Transformation of Banking Ecosystems in the Context of Fintech
AB  - In the context of technological progress, the use of payment solutions in virtual and augmented reality environments is also on the rise. Although these methods are still predominantly applied within educational and gaming platforms, their broader adoption across other sectors is anticipated. Personalization of banking offers and in-depth customer segmentation are likewise considered innovative trends in the sector. For instance, the development of banking applications tailored specifically for children contributes to the expansion of the client base. Within the evolution of banking ecosystems, chatbots have become widely utilized, performing a variety of functions ranging from account opening to tax payments. Nevertheless, despite their efficiency, some clients remain skeptical, perceiving chatbots as incapable of addressing more complex issues. Banking applications have also introduced so-called “stories” information platforms, which deliver banking news, financial literacy content, as well as services related to insurance and ticket sales. Another recent trend is the Open Banking concept, which provides third-party organizations with access to non-personalized banking data in order to enhance customer-centricity. This approach fosters competition, broadens opportunities for data analytics, and creates new avenues for business development.
