TI  - A Study on Consumer Perception towards Ai-Driven Financial Services in Sivakasi
AB  - In the last few years, Financial Services firms have rapidly begun using Artificial Intelligence (AI) to revolutionise how customers interact with their Banks and Financial Services. Some examples of AI enabled Financial Services are Chatbots, Robo Advisory Platforms, Fraud Detection systems, and AI-based automated Customer Care. In this study, we will investigate how consumers in Sivakasi view AI-enabled Financial Services concerning their level of Awareness about AI-enabled Financial Services, how many consumers are using these services, what they see as benefits of using them, trustworthiness, security, and overall satisfaction associated with using these services. Primary data will be collected from consumers using structured questionnaires, and we will analyse responses using appropriate statistical tools. The results of this research will show that consumers generally see AI enabled Financial Services as convenient to use and save time when performing routine banking transactions. Consumers do have concerns about the privacy and security of their data and the absence of a human representative when dealing with their bank. The study analyzes how demographics affect perceptions of AI-enabled financial services in Sivakasi and supports banks in improving AI adoption strategies while contributing to regional fintech consumer behavior research.
