TI  - Artificial Intelligence for Financial Inclusion and Digital Banking
AB  - Artificial Intelligence (AI) has emerged as a transformative technology in the banking and financial services sector, playing a vital role in promoting financial inclusion and accelerating the growth of digital banking. AI-driven technologies such as machine learning, natural language processing, predictive analytics, and big data analytics enable financial institutions to provide efficient, secure, and personalized financial services. This study examines the role of AI in expanding access to banking services for underserved and unbanked populations and explores its major applications in digital banking, including chatbots, digital payments, credit scoring, fraud detection, robo-advisory services, and mobile banking. AI facilitates improved customer experiences, enhanced risk management, increased credit accessibility, and reduced operational costs, thereby contributing to economic empowerment and sustainable development. Despite these benefits, challenges such as data privacy concerns, cybersecurity threats, algorithmic bias, regulatory issues, and digital literacy gaps remain significant barriers to effective implementation. The study highlights the importance of responsible AI governance and collaborative efforts among policymakers, financial institutions, and technology providers to ensure inclusive and ethical financial innovation. The findings suggest that AI has the potential to create a more accessible, efficient, and sustainable financial ecosystem while strengthening financial inclusion and supporting long-term economic growth.
