TI  - Buddie.local: A Production Architecture for Personal AGI
AB  - We describe Buddie.local, a fully operational private multi-tier agentic AI operating system built and operated by a single individual on commodity home hardware. The system integrates live personal finance, health, energy, and productivity data, routing queries across five intelligence tiers from instant deterministic local computation to multi-model ensemble deliberation. We introduce the Karpathy Ensemble — a three-stage Council architecture in which five AI personas with distinct reasoning styles generate independent responses, conduct blind peer review, and synthesise a single concrete action recommendation. The system implements a cost-aware routing doctrine in which the majority of queries are resolved by local Polars computation at zero LLM cost. A self-extending capability pipeline allows the system to build permanent skills from unanswered queries. The architecture is validated independently by six major AI systems. We argue that personal AGI does not require cloud scale, venture funding, or a team — it requires the right architecture.
