TI  - Trust in Ai-based Stock Trading Apps among Mumbai B. Com Students – with Focus on Grow
AB  - Abstract This study looks at how B. Com students in Mumbai trust the Artificial Intelligence features on the Groww investment application. The way people invest in the stock market has changed a lot because of investment platforms. These platforms make investing easier, faster and cheaper. Groww is a popular fintech platform in India. It offers Artificial Intelligence based services like personalized investment advice, portfolio analysis, market insights and an Artificial Intelligence chatbot. Since investing money can be risky and requires people to share financial information it is important to understand how much students trust these Artificial Intelligence features. The research uses a design and looks at numbers to get answers. The researchers collected information from B. Com students in Mumbai using a questionnaire with choice questions. They also looked at research journals SEBI reports, RBI publications, KPMG reports and other academic sources for information. They used tools like percentage analysis, mean, standard deviation, correlation and simple regression to see how ease of use, transparency, data privacy and trust in Artificial Intelligence are related. The study found that students are more likely to trust Growws Artificial Intelligence features when the application is easy to use explains how it makes recommendations and keeps financial data safe. The study also found that knowing about money and investing is important. Students who know about investing use Artificial Intelligence as a tool to help them not, as the way to make decisions. The research gives ideas to fintech companies, teachers and policymakers to make Artificial Intelligence based investment platforms better and to encourage young investors to invest digitally in a responsible way.
