TI  - FHAT Technical Note #004: Resistance Decay, Breakout, and Intraday Reversal — An Ex-Ante Documented Historical Case Study of SOXL on August 7, 2026
AB  - This technical note reconstructs an ex-ante documented historical case study surrounding a high-resistance zone in the Direxion Daily Semiconductor Bull 3X Shares (SOXL) on August 7, 2026. Abstract & Case Overview:Prior to the trading session, two competing hypotheses were retained in advance:1. H1 (Rejection): Sharp rejection at the 1-hour MA500 ($141.30 – $142.00) resistance zone.2. H2 (Resistance Decay): A breakout enabled by repeated testing, a flattening moving average slope, and timing convergence.3. H3 (Sequential Combination): An ordered combination where a breakout (H2) occurs first, followed by intraday instability and reversal (H1). The observed market path combined both hypotheses in sequence (H3): price crossed the declining 1-hour MA500, exceeded the prior high ($144.34) to reach $146.087, subsequently reversed to $131.56 (near Pivot Point $131.03), and recovered to approximately $140.25 at the close. Key Methodological Contributions:- Ex-Ante Scenario Freezing: Strictly separates contemporaneous observations from ex-post retrospective interpretation.- Transparent Error Reconciliation: Discloses explicit point deviations (+$0.287 on upper breakout, -$1.440 on lower pullback) and acknowledges untriggered extension scenarios (R2 at $150.28).- Evidence Hierarchy: Treats inverse-ETF (SOXS) mirror signals and platform-classified money-flow metrics strictly as auxiliary indicators rather than independent causal proof.- Human-AI Collaboration: Demonstrates language calibration standards and the role of LLMs as structured challengers in financial research. Document Metadata:- Document ID: FHAT-TN-004- Author: Yingshan Han (FHAT Independent Researcher)- Version: 1.0.2026-08-09- Classification: Technical Note / Historical Case Study (Not Peer Reviewed) Disclaimer: This document is for educational and research purposes only. It does not constitute investment advice or trading guidance.
