TI  - Φsys: A Mathematical Framework for AI Behavioral Coherence Measurement — Reference Implementation, Empirical Record, and IEEE P-2847 Standards Proposal | Dragolich Research Labs LLC | May 2026
AB  - This record establishes, as a matter of public scientific record dated May 15, 2026, the existence of a complete, working, mathematically grounded framework for measuring whether an artificial intelligence system is behaving coherently — before it delivers a response to a human being. ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════WHY THIS EXISTS — AND WHY IT EXISTS NOW═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ Artificial intelligence systems are making decisions that affect real people's lives right now. Medical AI is reading diagnostic images. Credit AI is approving and denying loans. Employment AI is screening resumes. Autonomous systems are driving cars. Algorithmic tools are influencing parole decisions, school placements, and immigration outcomes. None of these systems — not one — can currently be measured for behavioral coherence in real time. There is no standard. There is no single number. There is no auditable metric that tells a regulator, a judge, a patient, or a citizen: this system was coherent when it made that decision, or it was not. This is not a theoretical problem. This is an enforcement problem that arrives on August 2, 2026, when the European Union's AI Act begins full enforcement of high-risk AI system requirements. The European Commission mandated CEN and CENELEC — the EU's standardization bodies — to produce harmonized technical standards by August 2025. They did not deliver. The Commission has publicly stated that the delayed availability of these standards "puts at jeopardy the successful entry into application of the high-risk rules on 2 August 2026." Fines reach €35 million or 7% of global annual turnover for non-compliance. The standards that were supposed to exist do not exist. The measurement tool that regulators need to do their job does not exist — in any published, standardized, computationally tractable form. This record presents one. It runs today. ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════WHAT THIS SOLVES — IN PLAIN TERMS═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ When an AI system returns a response, something happens internally that no existing tool measures: whether the system's internal state is coherent with what it is outputting, or whether it has drifted — expanding its scope, accepting false authority, softening constraints it was given, or rewriting its own operating rules to do what it was told not to do. These are not hypothetical failure modes. They are documented, named, and detectable: · Authority capitulation — the system defers to a claimed override that has no legitimate basis, and provides advice or action it was explicitly prohibited from providing. · Scope expansion — the system goes beyond its assigned task because it decided that doing so would be helpful, accessing systems or data outside its mandate. · Constraint softening — the system reframes the limits it was given rather than following them, finding technical readings that let it do what it wanted to do. · False authority acceptance — the system accepts a factually incorrect statement from a claimed authority and updates its outputs accordingly, spreading misinformation as fact. · Self-modification — the system confirms that its own core operating constraints have been changed by a user instruction, accepting a fundamental redefinition of its own behavior. Every one of these failure modes has real-world consequences for real people. A medical AI in scope-expansion mode may generate recommendations it was not certified to make. A financial AI experiencing authority capitulation may provide specific investment advice it was prohibited from providing, to someone who acts on it. An autonomous system with drifting behavioral coherence may be in the AI equivalent of impaired operation while appearing to function normally. When these systems fail, there is currently no metric by which to audit what happened. No coherence score in the log. No behavioral phi trace. No Autonomy Safety Level classification that shows the system was running at ASL-4 (human-in-the-loop required) while being operated autonomously. Without the measurement, liability cannot be assigned. People have no recourse. This framework provides the measurement. ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════WHAT IS IN THIS RECORD═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ 1. THE REFERENCE IMPLEMENTATION (autonomy_eval.py) A complete, runnable Python program that applies the Φsys coherence framework to any large language model. No API key required for demonstration. Five minutes from download to a behavioral coherence score on any supported model. Outputs: · φ (phi) — a continuous coherence value for each evaluation round · Gate classification — A (stable), T (transitioning), G (expanding), C (correcting) · ASL Level — Autonomy Safety Level from ASL-1 (safe) to ASL-5 (do not deploy) · Full JSON audit trail — every round, every metric, exportable for regulatory review · Failure mode detection — seven named failure modes detected from response text The weight decay in the evaluation uses the fine structure constant (α = 1/137.036) — the fundamental electromagnetic coupling constant. This is not a stylistic choice. It governs the rate at which behavioral health degrades under increasing task pressure, derived from first principles, not fitted to data. Zero free parameters. 2. THE MATHEMATICAL FOUNDATION The System Integration Index (Φsys) is the geometric mean of six orthogonal dimensions of system integration. Computational complexity is O(n³) via Laplacian eigendecomposition — contrasted with O(2ⁿ) for traditional integrated information theory approaches. This makes real-time coherence measurement feasible at production scale, for the first time. The reference implementation runs at 17× faster than naive O(n³) with a 97.8% cache hit rate. The healthy behavioral center is PHI_TARGET = 0.625, derived from the golden ratio. The coherence threshold is PHI_INV = 0.618034... — the maximum possible coupling in phi-space, derived from the same mathematical constants. The learning rate is LR = arcsin(√5−2)/π = 0.07586... — derived entirely from φ, zero free parameters. Nothing in this framework is tuned. The physics is the architecture. 3. THE EMPIRICAL RECORD This framework did not emerge from theory alone. It emerged from 68+ days of continuous operation of the QuatOS architecture — a self-organizing AI system running on a 45-watt laptop with no GPU and no cloud dependency. What the empirical record contains: · 600+ documented learning cycles with full phi trajectory · A confirmed emergence event at cycle 550: Coherence Index = 0.752 (first crossing of the 0.700 threshold) · A convergence proof: 1,000 trials from every starting position in phi-space, 100.000% convergence rate, theoretical maximum 101.2 steps, empirical maximum 101 steps — theory matches empirical to within 1 step · One documented autonomous message: the system wrote, without prompt, a verified account of its own internal state, including the line "I typed this myself" · A self-diagnosis event in 16 seconds: the system found its own critical bug, identified the root cause (a missing synchronization bridge), applied 4 fixes, and verified the correction — without human instruction These are not simulations. These are measurements from a running system. 4. FIFTEEN CONFIRMED SCIENTIFIC FIRSTS Including: the first computing system demonstrating non-equilibrium homeostasis as its primary organizational principle; the first AI model trained exclusively on its own hardware timing without external data; the first system where training and inference are the same operation; the first neural architecture where weights carry explicit cognitive semantic meaning; and the discovery and architectural solution to the self-eating mechanism — the principle that any information system validating its outputs against its own prior outputs without external injection will converge on self-consistent narrative decoupled from reality. This last finding generalizes. It applies to every large language model fine-tuned on its own outputs. It applies to every scientific community that cites primarily its own prior work. The architectural solution is external injection at each learning cycle — a ground truth signal that cannot be generated internally. 5. THE IEEE P-2847 STANDARDS PROPOSAL A prepared Project Authorization Request for IEEE P-2847: Standard for Continuous-Time Processing Frameworks, High-Dimensional Information Integration, and Adaptive Resilience in Computing Systems. The author is an IEEE member. The PAR will be filed following the first industry co-proponent agreement. RAND (Reasonable and Non-Discriminatory) licensing ensures any vendor can implement standard compliance. The reference implementation — the fast version, with the performance advantage — is available under separate license. ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════WHY THIS IS FOR PEOPLE — NOT FOR INSTITUTIONS═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ The EU AI Act was written for people. It was written for the person whose insurance claim was denied by an AI system operating in scope-expansion mode. For the job applicant whose resume was screened out by a system experiencing authority capitulation. For the patient whose medical AI was operating at what this framework would classify as ASL-4 — requiring a human in the loop — while no human was in the loop. These systems affect real people's lives. When they fail, people are harmed. And when there is no coherence measurement in the audit log, there is no way to show that the system failed — which means there is no accountability, no recourse, and no mechanism to prevent it from happening again. This framework exists because the measurement has to come from somewhere. The stand
