TI  - AI Persona-as-a-Software™ Community Trilogy 1.0 (EVA, EINY, STARK) – Public Standard, Starter Kits and Launch Bundle
AB  - This OSF component publishes the AI Persona-as-a-Software™ (AI PaaS) Community Trilogy 1.0 – three governed community personas (EVA 1.0, EINY 1.0, STARK 1.0) plus their public standard, starter kits, and launch bundle. It represents the second major public release in the MasterMindGenesis / AI Persona-as-a-Software™ line of work, building directly on the earlier component “Persona-as-a-Software - AI PaaS Public Release and Licensing”, which introduced the core AI PaaS concept, governance model, and licensing framework. Contents This component includes: AI PaaS Community Trilogy Whitepaper (R): – Defines the AI Persona-as-a-Software™ Community Trilogy (EVA, EINY, STARK), the four pillars of PaaS, the role of Human Frequency Markup Language (HFML), and the governance boundaries of each persona. Persona Plug-N-Play Starter Kits (R): – EVA1.0-PaaS_PlugNPlay_Starter_Kit_R.zip – EINY1.0-PaaS_PlugNPlay_Starter_Kit_R.zip – STARK1.0-PaaS_PlugNPlay_Starter_Kit_R.zip Each starter kit contains the canonical community boot prompt for one persona, a minimal HFML user guide, a 60-second install guide, an official-status note, and a sharing template. These kits are designed to be: Portable across multiple AI hosts (custom GPTs, custom assistants, local LLM UIs, etc.) Governed, with strict non-clinical / non-advisory boundaries Standardized under the Community Trilogy framework. AI PaaS Trilogy Public Launch Bundle – A curated public package including: 0_README_START_HERE and user QuickStart: Standard artefacts (HFML mini-spec excerpts, forking/badge guidance, template persona config) Evidence index for cross-model testing of the starter kits High-level governance and investor briefs. Enterprise-grade Community Master Packs (EVA/EINY/STARK) are not included here and remain available only under separate NDA / licensing agreements. This component focuses on the public standard, community starter kits, and documentation needed for experimentation, teaching, and research. Relationship to earlier AI PaaS releases The November 2025 component “Persona-as-a-Software - AI PaaS Public Release and Licensing” introduced: The original AI PaaS whitepaper and licensing model standard The “AI PaaS vs present AI models” framing paper. This Community Trilogy 1.0 component: Turns that conceptual and licensing groundwork into installable, governed personas (EVA/EINY/STARK), Standardizes a minimal HFML interaction layer for end users, Publishes a public launch bundle with evidence and high-level governance context. Together, these components document the evolution from PaaS concept + licensing to a concrete, cross-platform, community-deployable Persona-as-a-Software™ standard. Intended audiences Researchers and practitioners exploring persona-level AI governance, prompt standardization, and cross-model behavior. Developers and builders who want a portable, governed starting point for life, reality-check, and financial-clarity personas. Governance, safety, and policy stakeholders interested in persona-level guardrails, HFML workflows, and cost-aware routing models. All materials in this component are provided for research, experimentation, and non-advisory educational use, and do not constitute medical, legal, or financial advice.
