TI  - DELTΔX NextGenV6 Speed — Non-Autonomous AI Governance Framework
AB  - DELTΔX NextGenV6 Speed Non-Autonomous AI Governance Framework DELTΔX NextGenV6 Speed is a non-autonomous AI-assisted governance framework created and authored by Jérôme Natalis and published by DELTΔX Editions. This OSF project provides a public documentary and research-oriented record of the DELTΔX NextGenV6 Speed corpus. OSF DOI: 10.17605/OSF.IO/TXU3V License: Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivatives 4.0 International — CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 Contact: deltax.editions@gmail.com --- Purpose DELTΔX NextGenV6 Speed is designed to support structured AI governance, evidence mapping, risk analysis, contradiction control, auditability, monitoring, recertification, and human decision support. The framework organizes complex AI-assisted reasoning without transferring decision authority to the AI system. It is a structuring framework. It is not an autonomous agent. It does not decide. It does not autonomously execute actions. It does not certify. It does not replace qualified experts. It does not validate real-world facts, legal compliance, medical validity, engineering safety, financial soundness, regulatory conformity, or institutional approval by itself. Final interpretation, responsibility, validation, and decision-making remain human. --- Return-to-reality discipline DELTΔX is designed to prevent AI outputs from becoming falsely certain. It separates: evidence from assumptions; risk from confidence; sources from proof; scores from truth; internal coherence from real-world validation; AI output from human decision. It forces important outputs back toward evidence, traceability, contradiction, risk, measurement, human responsibility, and real-world validation where required. It helps detect cases where: a score is treated as truth; a benchmark is treated as certification; a simulation is treated as field validation; AI consensus is treated as external proof; internal coherence is treated as real-world validation; human review is only formal; governance exists on paper but fails in practice; a system controls its own evidence, logs, metrics, audit scope, or validation path. The goal is not to make AI appear safer. The goal is to prevent AI from exceeding what evidence, traceability, reality, and human authority actually allow. --- Scope of use The DELTΔX corpus may support: AI governance; audit preparation; evidence mapping; risk analysis; contradiction management; controlled research; non-certifying technical framing; non-certifying legal framing; deployment review; monitoring design; incident review; recertification planning; human decision packets. This corpus is not a substitute for legal review, clinical validation, financial audit, engineering certification, regulatory approval, institutional authorization, or professional responsibility. --- Corpus structure The full NextGenV6 Speed version includes the current DELTΔX corpus with complementary layers. 1. DELTΔX Ω-ENGINE Central governance engine for admission control, human authority control, safety gates, evidence classification, risk status, traceability, contradiction handling, M/B/I/D separation, audit readiness, anti-drift logic, rollback, and recertification. 2. ANNEXE Ω-RDC-PLS-V5 Specialized annex for sensitive contexts involving Preventive LifeScore, health prevention, personal data, social data, profiling risk, insurance risk, public policy, public-health prevention, bias, monitoring, audit, and recertification. It separates prevention from profiling and blocks interpretation of scores as moral ranking, automated exclusion, insurance individualization, coercive classification, or hidden decision-making. 3. Ω-FORMAT-RIGOR-V1 Controlled output-format layer designed to keep evidence, uncertainty, assumptions, limits, risks, contradictions, auditability, recertification, and human decision authority visible. --- Base version The Base NextGen Speed version contains only the DELTΔX Ω-ENGINE document. It provides the foundational non-autonomous governance structure for admission control, authority control, evidence classification, risk routing, contradiction handling, audit trace, anti-drift logic, recertification, and human-controlled decision support. It does not include the full Preventive LifeScore annex. It does not include the full Ω-FORMAT-RIGOR output layer. --- OSF deposit notice This OSF project is a public documentary archive and research-oriented deposit. The OSF DOI and repository metadata may support citation, traceability, version identification, public availability, and authorship chronology. The repository is a documentary record, not a guarantee of originality, legal protection, technical validity, enforceability, or operational safety. The OSF deposit is not a commercial access page. The OSF deposit is not an operational deployment. The OSF deposit is not a certification, legal opinion, regulatory approval, institutional endorsement, medical validation, engineering validation, financial advice, or authorization for autonomous use. The OSF deposit does not grant rights beyond the license and restrictions stated in the uploaded documents and this project description. --- License notice The uploaded DELTΔX materials are governed by: Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivatives 4.0 International — CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 The OSF license selector may not display the exact CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 option. If the exact option is unavailable, the governing license remains the license stated in the uploaded documents and in this project description. Non-commercial sharing of the unmodified documents with proper attribution is permitted. No derivative use, modified redistribution, commercial use, SaaS/API integration, GPT/chatbot reproduction, prompt-package reuse, model-training reuse, operational deployment, certification service, consulting product, institutional use, or official adaptation is authorized without prior written permission from Jérôme Natalis / DELTΔX Editions. All rights not expressly granted under the stated license remain reserved. License URL: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/ --- No waiver and no implied license expansion Public availability of these materials on OSF does not constitute a waiver of rights. It does not authorize extraction, adaptation, commercial reuse, derivative implementation, system cloning, model training, institutional deployment, operational deployment, or certification services beyond the stated license. Failure by the rights holder to immediately object to an unauthorized use must not be interpreted as consent, authorization, waiver, abandonment, or license expansion. All rights not expressly granted remain reserved. --- Anti-misrepresentation notice No person, organization, AI system, chatbot, SaaS platform, workflow, service, institution, benchmark, certification offer, or commercial product may claim to be an official DELTΔX implementation, certified system, authorized deployment, official fork, official partner, or validated continuation without prior written authorization from Jérôme Natalis / DELTΔX Editions. Unauthorized uses include, but are not limited to: removal of attribution; removal of license terms; false authorship claim; false affiliation; commercial reuse without permission; derivative implementation without permission; modified redistribution; GPT / chatbot reproduction; SaaS or API integration; prompt-package resale; model-training reuse; operational deployment; certification claim; institutional claim; confusingly similar presentation. --- Research-use limitation This OSF deposit is provided for documentary, citation, research-reference, audit-reference, and non-commercial access purposes. It is not provided as executable software. It is not provided as a deployable system. It is not provided as a compliance product. It is not provided as a medical, legal, financial, engineering, regulatory, or institutional authority. Any real-world use requires independent review, competent human responsibility, domain-specific validation, and written authorization where required. --- Recommended citation Natalis, J. DELTΔX NextGenV6 Speed — Non-Autonomous AI Governance Framework. DELTΔX Editions. OSF DOI: 10.17605/OSF.IO/TXU3V --- Core principle AI structures. Human decides. Reality validates. Measurement falsifies. Trace audits. Contradiction triggers control. Drift triggers STOP. --- DELTΔX NextGenV6 Speed Cadre de gouvernance IA non autonome DELTΔX NextGenV6 Speed est un cadre de gouvernance IA assisté par IA, non autonome, créé et rédigé par Jérôme Natalis et publié par DELTΔX Editions. Ce projet OSF constitue une trace documentaire publique et un dépôt orienté recherche du corpus DELTΔX NextGenV6 Speed. DOI OSF : 10.17605/OSF.IO/TXU3V Licence : Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivatives 4.0 International — CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 Contact : deltax.editions@gmail.com --- Objet DELTΔX NextGenV6 Speed est conçu pour soutenir la gouvernance structurée de l’IA, la cartographie des preuves, l’analyse des risques, le contrôle des contradictions, l’auditabilité, le monitoring, la recertification et le support à la décision humaine. Le cadre organise le raisonnement complexe assisté par IA sans transférer l’autorité décisionnelle au système IA. Il s’agit d’un cadre structurant. Ce n’est pas un agent autonome. Il ne décide pas. Il n’exécute pas d’actions de manière autonome. Il ne certifie pas. Il ne remplace pas les experts qualifiés. Il ne valide pas par lui-même les faits réels, la conformité juridique, la validité médicale, la sécurité ingénierique, la solidité financière, la conformité réglementaire ou l’approbation institutionnelle. L’interprétation finale, la responsabilité, la validation et la décision restent humaines. --- Discipline de retour au réel DELTΔX est conçu pour empêcher les sor
